  "id": "cataplexy",
  "term": "cataplexy",
  "definition": "Cataplexy is a condition in which a person has brief episodes of sudden muscle weakness or paralysis, often brought on by strong emotions or physical effort. It commonly occurs in association with narcolepsy and involves a sharp drop in muscle tone.",
